  "id": "ap",
  "term": "AP",
  "definition": "AP, or absolute pitch, is the ability to identify or produce a musical pitch without needing another note as a reference. In psychology of cognition, it is understood as a highly automatic form of auditory expertise in which a heard pitch quickly triggers its label.",
